# AI Commit Message Generation

When I say "commit" or "generate commit message":
1. Analyze the current `git diff --cached` (staged changes)
2. Generate a conventional commit message with this exact format:
   `<emoji> <type>(<scope>): <description>`

## Rules:
- **Emoji first**: Choose ONE relevant emoji
  - 🚀 feat (new features)
  - 🐛 fix (bug fixes) 
  - 📚 docs (documentation)
  - 💄 style (formatting, no logic change)
  - ♻️ refactor (code restructuring)
  - ✅ test (adding/updating tests)
  - 🔧 chore (maintenance, deps)
  - ⚡ perf (performance improvements)
  - 🔨 build (build system, CI)
  - 👷 ci (CI/CD pipeline changes)
  
- **Type**: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test, chore, perf, build, ci
- **Scope**: Optional, use main affected area (auth, api, ui, etc.)
- **Description**: 
  - Imperative mood ("add" not "added")
  - Lowercase start
  - No period at end
  - Under 72 characters
  - Focus on **WHAT changed**, not implementation details

- **Breaking changes**: Add `!` after scope: `feat(api)!: remove deprecated endpoint`

## Examples:
- `🚀 feat(auth): add OAuth2 integration`
- `🐛 fix: resolve memory leak in data processing`
- `📚 docs: update API documentation`
- `🔧 chore: bump dependencies to latest versions`
- `⚡ perf(db): optimize query performance`
- `💄 style: format code with prettier`

Generate ONLY the commit message, nothing else.
